# tally 2.2.1 P36, B5 and Q7 (L §5.19 l.1717, "disagree on an amount or a day"): two rows stated same that
# disagree only on the day warn, (<a>) and (<b>) their days (review g2 lead/w2_day_only). Before W8: no warning.
=== w2_day_only.tally
model w2
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-04-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
input bank: observed
input sbank: observed

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 1000.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

ask b_k: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask b_s: bal(sav, 2026-03-31)
ask n: count(t in transfers over 2026-03)

version st_k
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-02
  covers konto
  bank[a1] = (on: 2026-03-18, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to sav amount 950.00 PLN) "konto line"

version st_s
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-03
  covers sav
  sbank[b1] = (on: 2026-03-19, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to sav amount 950.00 PLN) "sav line"
  same bank[a1] = sbank[b1]
=== expect
b_k: 50.00 PLN
  cut 2026-04-10
b_s: 950.00 PLN
  cut 2026-04-10
n: 1
  cut 2026-04-10
warning: WARN-LEGS the two observations of bank[a1] disagree: bank[a1] (2026-03-18) and sbank[b1] (2026-03-19)
